// Optional site settings for Perlmutter, used as `pixi run pipeline ... -c /path/site.config`.
// Keep your copy outside the checkout. The nersc profile is selected automatically there.
//
// Account: jobs are charged to your default NERSC project. For another one, set it in your
// shell (export SBATCH_ACCOUNT=PROJECT) rather than in process.clusterOptions, which would
// replace the profile's QOS and memory settings.
//
// QOS: the profile uses `shared` (at most half a node, 48 h). Change it with --queue, or
// for one run with SBATCH_QOS. Long Nextflow manager runs belong in NERSC's workflow QOS.
//
// Work defaults to $SCRATCH/workspace, which NERSC purges; output and trace files to
// $CFS/PROJECT/$USER/runs/RUN_NAME. Pass -P/--persist-dir to `pixi run pipeline` for another
// folder; setting params.persist_dir here comes too late, as nextflow.config derives the paths
// first.
// References default to $CFS/PROJECT/$USER/references (PROJECT: your default Slurm
// account); pass -R/--references to `pixi run pipeline` to use another folder. (The wrapper
// passes it to Nextflow as --references, which takes precedence over params set in this file.)
